From 70f053d89212b5ecd0f43f9ff724d79bf0bb7eeb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 23:17:27 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] feat(post): pause or home after an operation; suppress
 ops; skip pauses and homes

Each operation now carries an after-action (Operation.after, the post
crate's AfterOperation): Continue (default), Optional stop, Program stop
or Go home. Continue is the stream's silent default, so every CL/NC
golden stays byte-exact.

- Stream: any other choice rides one PARAM AfterOperation
  optional-stop|stop|home ahead of the section (the #112 coolant
  pattern).
- Posts: afterOp() writes the dialect's words after the section's
  spindle stop. Fanuc/Haas/Mazak M1 / M0, home G91 G28 Z0, G28 X0 Y0,
  G90. Siemens 840D M1 / M0, home G0 G53 Z0 then G0 G53 X0 Y0. Fanuc
  Lathe M01 / M00, home G28 U0 then G28 W0. Heidenhain M1 / M0; a
  Heidenhain home is a counted message() naming the post (#50: no
  machine-referenced home it can trust), so the gate blocks it.
- Suppress: Operation.suppressed. posting::program_ops drops suppressed
  ops before the freshness law, so the post, the program sim and the
  limit check all skip them. The toolpath and stamp are kept. If every
  op is suppressed, the post refuses by name.
- Skip pauses and homes: a PostOptions singleton switched by the
  undoable SetPostOptions command (a checkbox under the Post picker).
  It mutes every after-action at post; the ops keep their choices.
- Commands: EditOperationParams::with_after / with_suppressed, one
  undo unit each.
- UI: the op context menu gets "Suppress operation" / "Unsuppress
  operation" and an "After: ..." row that steps through the choices.
  The tree row shows SUPPRESSED / "then <action>".
- Project file: "after", "suppressed" and the top-level "skip_stops"
  are written only off their defaults; older files load with the
  defaults, no version bump.

Standalone Pause / Home list entries are owed: #155.

Fixes #110

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
